{"type":"message","id":"0e2e0323","parentId":"2fca5a14","timestamp":"2026-06-02T11:32:32.602Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API returned error code 1101 for both requests. This might be a Cloudflare Workers error code (1101 = \"Worker threw exception\"). The POST endpoint might not exist or there's an issue with the request format. Let me check the API endpoint more carefully - maybe the send endpoint has a different path or the error is about the request body format.\n\nActually, 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an exception\" - something wrong on the server side. But wait, the GET endpoints work fine. Let me try without the JSON content-type or with a different format.\n\nWait, the error might be that the send endpoint requires a different path. Let me check if there's a different way to call it.","thinkingSignature":"3e3fc8184a79232fae0bf9bc405846c869c13244f0c86359c77326f6fbd1fc83"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_vetqltyu1czt_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 11:30 UTC]**\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":6997,"output":249,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20928,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780399947508,"responseId":"066df24ca2209dd4added708ff9174e2"}}
